      <title>tangoGPS: from Gtk development to Openmoko app.</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Lightning Talks</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The interesting part of the app is the fact that it is&#xA;entirely developed on a desktop machine set up for GNOME development&#xA;without anything special and the resulting app simply needs to be&#xA;recompiled in order to run under OpenMoko on the FIC Neo1973 phone. The&#xA;talk will thus focus on the ease with which any Gtk-developer can&#xA;develop for Openmoko literally in minutes.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Current Project Version: 0.1, fully functional, loading automatically&#xA;maps from OpenStreetMaps and displaying them, plus location cursor and track.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
